/*
    Ragged parent-child rep hierarchy, flattened with PATH (requirement #8).
    Dim Employee: EmployeeKey, ManagerKey (self-referencing), varying depth
    by region (ragged - some reps report directly to a Regional Director,
    others go through an intermediate Team Lead).

    These are CALCULATED COLUMNS on Dim Employee, computed once at refresh,
    not measures - hierarchy levels need to exist as columns to build a
    browsable hierarchy in the field list.
*/

-- Calculated column: full path from root to this employee, as a delimited string of keys
EmployeePath =
PATH ( Dim_Employee[EmployeeKey], Dim_Employee[ManagerKey] )

-- Calculated column: how deep this employee sits (used to detect raggedness)
EmployeePathLength =
PATHLENGTH ( Dim_Employee[EmployeePath] )

-- Calculated columns: fixed-depth levels for a browsable hierarchy.
-- PATHITEM returns BLANK beyond an employee's actual depth, which is exactly
-- the "ragged" behavior wanted - a Level 3 rep under a 2-level chain just
-- shows blank at Level 4+, Power BI's hierarchy visual naturally collapses that.
Level 1 (Top) =
PATHITEM ( Dim_Employee[EmployeePath], 1, TEXT )

Level 2 =
PATHITEM ( Dim_Employee[EmployeePath], 2, TEXT )

Level 3 =
PATHITEM ( Dim_Employee[EmployeePath], 3, TEXT )

Level 4 =
PATHITEM ( Dim_Employee[EmployeePath], 4, TEXT )

-- Measure: roll up a rep's own Net Revenue plus everyone below them in the chain
Team Net Revenue :=
VAR CurrentManagerKey = SELECTEDVALUE ( Dim_Employee[EmployeeKey] )
VAR TeamMembers =
    FILTER (
        ALL ( Dim_Employee ),
        PATHCONTAINS ( Dim_Employee[EmployeePath], CurrentManagerKey )
    )
RETURN
    CALCULATE ( [Net Revenue], TeamMembers )
-- Description: Net Revenue for this employee plus their entire downline,
-- regardless of how many levels deep the chain goes - this is what makes
-- the hierarchy "ragged-safe": a Team Lead with 2 reports and a Director
-- with 40 reports across 3 levels both get a correct roll-up from the same
-- measure, no per-level special-casing.

/*
    Build the user-facing hierarchy in the model as:
    Hierarchy "Management Chain": Level 1 (Top) -> Level 2 -> Level 3 -> Level 4
    Drop [Team Net Revenue] on a matrix with that hierarchy on rows - it
    rolls up correctly at every level, including levels that don't exist for
    shallower branches.
*/
